# AGENT.md — src/

Application root.

## What lives here

- `main.ts` — starts the server{{#if hasOrm}} and initializes the ORM connection{{/if}}. Nothing else.
- `app.ts` — **composition root.** Wire every module's object graph here
  and nowhere else. Import this directly in tests (via supertest + `app.callback()`)
  instead of starting a real server.
- `config/` — environment loading{{#if useSwagger}} and Swagger setup{{/if}}.
- `middlewares/` — cross-cutting request handling (errors, validation glue)
  used by more than one route.
- `shared/` — cross-cutting infrastructure (database, cache{{#if useAuth}}, auth{{/if}}{{#if useHealthCheck}}, health{{/if}}) used by more
  than one module.
- `core/` — domain entities, repository ports (abstract interfaces), and
  use-cases. This layer has zero knowledge of Koa or any adapter.
- `adapters/` — concrete implementations of core ports. Controllers, routes,
  presenters, DTOs, and repository implementations live here.

## Rules

- Do not put business logic in `main.ts` or `app.ts`.
- When you add a new module, wire it in `app.ts` in the same change — an
  unwired controller is unreachable and fails silently.
- `core/` must never import from `adapters/`. The arrow points inward.
- Koa error handling differs from Express: the error middleware at the top of
  the stack catches all thrown errors automatically. No manual `next(err)`
  needed.
{{#if useAuth}}
- Auth middleware (`authenticate`) is imported from `shared/auth/auth.middleware`.
  Apply it as a per-route middleware in the router that needs protection.
{{/if}}
